From e21836a46dc8d615fe63abbe4eda30915878d1fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Z. Liu" <zhixu.liu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:29:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] cmake: define _LARGEFILE64_SOURCE

Define _LARGEFILE64_SOURCE to expose LFS64 interfaces such as
lseek64() and off64_t.

musl only provides these compatibility definitions when
_LARGEFILE64_SOURCE is defined. Defining _GNU_SOURCE alone is
not sufficient.

This fixes build failures on musl without adding libc-specific
compatibility definitions.

This was previously handled by Autotools but appears to have
been lost during the migration to CMake.

See also: https://github.com/ceph/ceph/pull/8402

Signed-off-by: Z. Liu <zhixu.liu@gmail.com>

diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
index 46226c6bbe8..86c19833e8c 100644
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -94,6 +94,7 @@ add_definitions(
 
 if(LINUX)
   add_definitions("-D_GNU_SOURCE")
+  add_definitions("-D_LARGEFILE64_SOURCE")
 endif()
 
 add_compile_options(
-- 
