Subject: [PATCH 2/5] pretty_binary: include cstdint for int32_t

pretty_binary.cc uses int32_t without explicitly including its
defining header. This happened to work due to transitive includes
on some standard library implementations, but fails on musl.

Include <cstdint> explicitly to avoid relying on transitive
header dependencies.

Signed-off-by: Z. Liu <zhixu.liu@gmail.com>

diff --git a/src/common/pretty_binary.cc b/src/common/pretty_binary.cc
index 62f68b3efa4..b2ee0a30369 100644
--- a/src/common/pretty_binary.cc
+++ b/src/common/pretty_binary.cc
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 // vim: ts=8 sw=2 sts=2 expandtab
 
 #include "pretty_binary.h"
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <stdexcept>
 #include <sstream>
 
-- 
