Subject: [PATCH 5/5] libcephfs_proxy: include <limits.h> explicitly for
 PATH_MAX

PATH_MAX is defined in <limits.h>. Although glibc exposes it
indirectly through <stdio.h>, musl requires <limits.h> to be
included explicitly.

Signed-off-by: Z. Liu <zhixu.liu@gmail.com>

diff --git a/src/libcephfs_proxy/proxy_mount.c b/src/libcephfs_proxy/proxy_mount.c
index aedaa5bc907..e9baa3e5e3c 100644
--- a/src/libcephfs_proxy/proxy_mount.c
+++ b/src/libcephfs_proxy/proxy_mount.c
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 #include "proxy_mount.h"
 #include "proxy_helpers.h"
 
+#include <limits.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <sys/stat.h>
